<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Stage 6 E12: hardened-runtime entitlements for the Developer ID
  signature. PaperWhirl is NOT sandboxed (Developer ID distribution
  outside the App Store), so there are no App Sandbox keys here — only
  the hardened-runtime exceptions our sidecar architecture requires:

    disable-library-validation
      The .app spawns a bundled python-build-standalone interpreter as a
      sidecar, which loads dylibs signed by other teams / ad-hoc (PBS,
      Playwright's Chromium, our @loader_path-rewritten Poppler dylibs).
      Library validation would block those loads. This is the load-bearing
      one — both the main shell and the python executable need it.

    allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      Chromium's V8 JIT (Playwright drives bundled headless Chromium for
      publisher scraping) maps executable pages. Required for its helper
      processes to launch under hardened runtime.

    allow-dyld-environment-variables
      The sidecar sets PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH and prepends Poppler's
      bin/ to PATH; embedded CPython may consult DYLD_* during dylib
      resolution. Permitting dyld env vars avoids hardened-runtime
      rejection of the spawned interpreter.

  These are applied to the Mach-O executables during the inside-out
  Developer ID sign in scripts/inject_python.sh.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
